{
  "name": "golden-002-promotion-ladder-and-supersession",
  "description": "Two threads climbing the ladder at different rates, two distinct retrieval contracts on the same target (meaning and reading are separate contracts, REQ-DM-05/T-05), observations at every tier, and a correction that supersedes a misgraded review. The superseded observation stays in the ledger with a marker rather than disappearing — history is never rewritten (REQ-DM-04.2) — and WP-06's gate keeps it out of the scheduler, so the correction corrects something rather than merely annotating it. The lookup, the tier-B production and the tier-D exposure are each recorded and refused by name (T-07, T-08). Only the reading contract's tier-A review reaches FSRS, which is T-05 in fixture form: the meaning contract's memory state stays untouched by a miss on the reading.",
